{"id":"80361b698fe23910c43b99986d86cd556fd49639","axis":"silent","repo":"argoproj/argo-cd","sha":"80361b698fe23910c43b99986d86cd556fd49639","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"assets/swagger.json","lines":["@@ -5808,6 +5808,9 @@","         \"resourceViewEnabled\": {","           \"type\": \"boolean\"","         },","+        \"ssoAutoLogin\": {","+          \"type\": \"boolean\"","+        },","         \"statusBadgeEnabled\": {","           \"type\": \"boolean\"","         },"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"common/common.go","lines":["@@ -130,6 +130,8 @@ const ("," \tAuthCookieName = \"argocd.token\""," \t// StateCookieName is the HTTP cookie name that holds temporary nonce tokens for CSRF protection"," \tStateCookieName = \"argocd.oauthstate\"","+\t// SSOAutoLoginPausedCookieName is the HTTP cookie name that tells the UI not to redirect to SSO after a logout","+\tSSOAutoLoginPausedCookieName = \"argocd.sso.autoLoginPaused\""," \t// StateCookieMaxAge is the maximum age of the oauth state cookie"," \tStateCookieMaxAge = time.Minute * 5"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/operator-manual/argocd-cm.yaml","lines":["@@ -384,6 +384,10 @@ data:","   # Optional override for the SSO login button label.","   # ui.loginButtonText: \"SSO Login\""," ","+  # Redirect the login page to the SSO provider without waiting for the user to click the SSO login button.","+  # Requires an OIDC provider or Dex connector. Open /login?sso_auto_login=false to reach the local login form.","+  # sso.autoLogin: \"false\"","+","   # Application reconciliation timeout is the amount of time spent before Argo tries to discover if a new manifests version got","   # published to the repository. Reconciliation by timeout is disabled if timeout is set to 0. Two minutes by default with additional jitter.","   # For the argocd-repo-server this setting defines the expiration"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/operator-manual/feature-maturity.md","lines":["@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ to indicate their stability and maturity. These are the statuses of non-stable f"," | [Service Account Impersonation][10]       | v2.13.0    | Beta   |"," | [Source Hydrator][11]                     | v2.14.0    | Beta   |"," | [ApplicationSet Web UI][12]               | v3.5.0     | Alpha  |","+| [Automatic SSO login][13]                 | v3.7.0     | Beta   |"," "," ## Unstable Configurations"," ","@@ -68,6 +69,7 @@ to indicate their stability and maturity. These are the statuses of non-stable f"," | [Source Hydrator][11]                     | `ConfigMap/argocd-cmd-params-cm`              | `hydrator.enabled`                                          | Beta   |"," | [Source Hydrator][11]                     | `Deployment/argocd-application-controller`    | `ARGOCD_HYDRATOR_ENABLED`                                   | Beta   |"," | [Source Hydrator][11]                     | `Deployment/argocd-server`                    | `ARGOCD_HYDRATOR_ENABLED`                                   | Beta   |","+| [Automatic SSO login][13]                 | `ConfigMap/argocd-cm`                         | `sso.autoLogin`                                             | Beta   |"," "," [2]: applicationset/Progressive-Syncs.md"," [3]: ../developer-guide/extensions/proxy-extensions.md","@@ -79,3 +81,4 @@ to indicate their stability and maturity. These are the statuses of non-stable f"," [10]: app-sync-using-impersonation.md"," [11]: ../user-guide/source-hydrator.md"," [12]: ../user-guide/application-set-ui.md","+[13]: user-management/index.md#automatic-sso-login"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/operator-manual/user-management/index.md","lines":["@@ -158,6 +158,51 @@ There are two ways that SSO can be configured:","   [Okta](okta.md), [OneLogin](onelogin.md), [Auth0](auth0.md), [Microsoft](microsoft.md), [Keycloak](keycloak.md),","   [Google (G Suite)](google.md)), where you manage your users, groups, and memberships."," ","+### Automatic SSO login","+","+> [!WARNING]","+> **Beta Feature (Since v3.7.0)**","+>","+> This is a [beta-quality](https://github.com/argoproj/argoproj/blob/main/community/feature-status.md#beta)","+> feature. The common cases work, but how the login page decides when to redirect may still change.","+","+By default, the login page shows an SSO login button that users have to click. To send users to the SSO provider as soon as","+they open the login page, set `sso.autoLogin` to `\"true\"` in the `argocd-cm` ConfigMap:","+","+```yaml","+apiVersion: v1","+kind: ConfigMap","+metadata:","+  name: argocd-cm","+  namespace: argocd","+data:","+  sso.autoLogin: \"true\"","+```","+","+The setting only takes effect when an OIDC provider or at least one Dex connector is configured. If more than one Dex","+connector is configured and `dex.auth.connectorId` is not set, users land on the Dex connector selection page. If","+anonymous access is enabled with `users.anonymous.enabled`, visitors who open the UI are not redirected and browse as the","+anonymous user. Clicking **Log in** takes them to the SSO provider, unless one of the cases below applies.","+","+The login page does not redirect automatically in the following cases:","+","+* Dex failed with a server error during the previous SSO attempt. The login page shows the error instead of redirecting","+  again, to avoid a redirect loop when Dex is not available. With an OIDC provider configured directly, a failed","+  login stops on an error page and does not return to the login page.","+* The user logged out, either from the Argo CD UI or by opening `/auth/logout`, or last logged in with a local account","+  such as `admin`. Without this, a user whose session with the identity provider is still active would be signed straight","+  back in, and a local account user whose session expired would be moved to their SSO identity. Auto-login resumes in that","+  browser after the next SSO login.","+* The browser blocks local storage. Argo CD needs it to remember logouts and local account logins, so it does not redirect","+  without it.","+* The login page URL contains `sso_auto_login=false`, for example `https://argocd.example.com/login?sso_auto_login=false`.","+  Use this to reach the username and password form, for instance to log in as the local `admin` user while SSO is not available.","+  If local logins are disabled, the page shows only the SSO login button.","+","+> [!NOTE]","+> Logging out of Argo CD does not end the session with the identity provider. To end both, also configure a","+> [logout URL for your OIDC provider](#configuring-a-custom-logout-url-for-your-oidc-provider).","+"," ## Dex"," "," Argo CD embeds and bundles [Dex](https://github.com/dexidp/dex) as part of its installation, for the"],"additions":45,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/apiclient/settings/settings.pb.go","lines":["@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ type Settings struct {"," \tSyncWithReplaceAllowed    bool                               `protobuf:\"varint,29,opt,name=syncWithReplaceAllowed,proto3\" json:\"syncWithReplaceAllowed,omitempty\"`"," \tUiLoginButtonText         string                             `protobuf:\"bytes,30,opt,name=uiLoginButtonText,proto3\" json:\"uiLoginButtonText,omitempty\"`"," \tResourceViewEnabled       bool                               `protobuf:\"varint,31,opt,name=resourceViewEnabled,proto3\" json:\"resourceViewEnabled,omitempty\"`","+\tSsoAutoLogin              bool                               `protobuf:\"varint,32,opt,name=ssoAutoLogin,proto3\" json:\"ssoAutoLogin,omitempty\"`"," \tXXX_NoUnkeyedLiteral      struct{}                           `json:\"-\"`"," \tXXX_unrecognized          []byte                             `json:\"-\"`"," \tXXX_sizecache             int32                              `json:\"-\"`","@@ -363,6 +364,13 @@ func (m *Settings) GetResourceViewEnabled() bool {"," \treturn false"," }"," ","+func (m *Settings) GetSsoAutoLogin() bool {","+\tif m != nil 